---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR_ROLE, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { organizationSchema, breadcrumbSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { PAGES } from '../../lib/guides';
import { helpers } from '../../lib/helpers';
const lang = 'en';
const h = helpers(lang);
const n = PAGES.length + 1;
---
<PageLayout title="Radif Partners, publisher of Behavior Tech Exam: who we are" description="Who publishes Behavior Tech Exam, how its practice questions, cost calculators and state rules are written and checked, and what the site will never sell." lang={lang} jsonLd={[organizationSchema(lang), profilePageSchema({ path: route('about', lang), lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path: route('about', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-600">About</p><h1 class="mt-0 text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Who is behind {SITE_NAMES[lang]}</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <div class="not-prose mb-6"><p class="text-lg font-semibold text-navy-900">{AUTHOR_NAME}</p><p class="text-navy-700">{AUTHOR_ROLE[lang]}</p></div>
    <p>{SITE_NAMES[lang]} is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that turns public rules and public data into free tools. This site serves people starting out in applied behavior analysis: new hires at ABA clinics who must pass the behavior technician exam within months of starting, paraprofessionals in schools, students who want a first credential before graduate school, and supervisors who onboard them.</p>
    <h2>What you will find here</h2>
    <p>A full mock in the published format, practice by outline domain and by topic with every answer explained, a review mode that brings back what you missed, the cost of certification with the fees of the states that add their own credential, the deadlines of the application and of the renewal, the monthly supervision arithmetic, the 2025 pass rates of training providers, and a short track for the analyst exam. All of it is free, with no account and no email address.</p>
    <h2>Where the content comes from</h2>
    <p>The {h.num(h.count)} practice questions are ours: each one trains one task of the public outline and quotes the task code, never the task wording at length. The fees, deadlines and rules were read in the certification board's handbooks and on the pages of the state boards, and each page links to the document behind it. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> explains how a mock is drawn and how the study target differs from the official result.</p>
    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>We are not the certification board, its test vendor, a state board, a training provider or an employer. We cannot see your account, approve an application, book a seat or sign a competency assessment. The site shows no official logo, and the clinical scenarios in the questions are exam content, not treatment advice.</p>
    <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
    <p>Nothing is sold here: no course, no study guide, no flash cards and no referral fee. If advertising appears one day, it will stay out of the quizzes and will never see your answers, which do not leave your browser.</p>
    <h2>Report a mistake</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the fee or the first words of the question. The <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> says how corrections are made and dated. The site has {n} pages.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600">Rules and fees last checked on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-US')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
